## ❓ Frequently Asked Questions

<details>
<summary><b>What are HTML5 games?</b></summary>

HTML5 games are games designed to work using web technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and browser APIs. Depending on the project, they may run directly in a browser or require a local development environment.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Do I need to install anything?</b></summary>

A hosted browser game may require only a browser. Projects distributed as source code may require additional tools or a local web server. Follow each project's setup instructions.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Can I modify the games?</b></summary>

For open-source projects, modification and redistribution depend on the license of each individual project. Review its license and any separate asset licenses first.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Are the games mobile-friendly?</b></summary>

Compatibility varies by project. Some games support touch controls and responsive layouts, while others are optimized for desktop browsers.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Can beginners learn from these projects?</b></summary>

Yes. HTML5 games can be useful examples for practicing JavaScript, user input, game loops, animation, and UI design. Beginner suitability depends on each project's complexity.

</details>

<br/>

<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreasbm/readme/master/assets/lines/rainbow.png" width="100%" alt="section divider"/>

## 📜 Licenses & Responsible Use

**Open source does not mean every project uses the same license.** Check the license, attribution requirements, and any separately licensed artwork, music, or other assets before copying, modifying, or distributing a game.


